==Strategy==
This stage is very easy to mess up if underprepared. Not only does Retsu come out on a strict timer, only giving you a single Celeboodle to prepare beforehand, he comes supported with dangerous enemies, including everyone's favorite midranger, R.Ost, appearing at 300%. Because of this, your main goal to win is to play defensively using [[Cyberpunk Cat]]. [[Haniwa Cat]], even at low levels, is able to tank a couple of hits from Retsu as well as the supporting enemies, and [[Thaumaturge Cat]] is great here to massively reduce R.Ost's pushing power. Do your best to kill each Dagshund that appears, because given his bulkiness it's very easy for your defense to falter. Use units like [[Jelly Dumpling Cat]], [[Bullet Train Cat]], [[Hitman Cat]] or [[Manic Macho Legs Cat]] to chip him down. Most importantly, conserve your cash carefully, as your only cash supply are infrequent Celeboodles who you won't be able to Double Bounty often. To that end, be careful of how much you spam your units, given that Retsu is able to wipe out your stacks very easily and leave you broke.

